uation.\nC. Saying \"I can't do this\" or \"I wish I could have more control\" would likely come across as unprofessional and may not resolve the problem with the coworker.\n\nThe best option, D, emphasizes maintaining professionalism and suggests walking away or taking deep breaths to regain composure before addressing the issue with the coworker. This approach minimizes the chance of escalation and gives you an opportunity to calmly discuss the situation."}]}
