x issue with far-reaching implications, both for the nation leaving the Union as well as for its neighbors. The possible negative impact on the NATO alliance, as warned by the senior US military commander, is one such concern that merits attention. The future effectiveness of NATO and its ability to maintain international peace and stability will largely depend on the alliance's adaptive capabilities and the commitment of its member countries. As the challenges posed by Brexit continue to unfold, cooperation and communication between nations will be crucial to ensuring that the bond between NATO members remains robust, secure, and faithful to its founding principles."}]}
