e following ideas in mind when reviewing your diet:  Try to steer clear of processed foods. Eat more whole foods instead, such as fruits, vegetables, whole grains, and lean proteins. Lower your intake of dairy products. Foods that are high in carbohydrates may trigger acne outbreaks. These include things like bread and pasta. .  Stress may also cause acne outbreaks, so it is important to keep your stress under control. Whenever possible, try to reduce the amount of stress in your daily life to help lessen the severity of any acne problem.  You might try meditation or exercise to lower stress. Going for a peaceful walk outdoors can be a good way to relax. If possible, avoid any situations that you find stressful.\n\nSummary:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Studies suggest that patients with acne may have lower stomach acid levels, and consuming bitter herbs with meals can help stimulate digestion and potentially reduce future acne outbreaks. Examples of bitter herbs are dandelion leaf, yarrow, wormwood, and gentian. Incorporating dark, bitter greens into meals can be beneficial. Rhassoul clay can also be used to reduce the chances of acne outbreaks without harming the skin. A healthy diet, consisting of whole foods and lower carbohydrate intake, can help reduce the severity and frequency of outbreaks. Additionally, managing stress through meditation, exercise, or peaceful walks can also play a role in reducing acne problems."}]}
