und), it might hamper the development of the necessary electrical potential for a lightning strike. In this case, lightning could become less frequent or less powerful, as the charges may not reach the threshold needed to initiate a discharge.\n\nOn the contrary, if the imbalance between negative and positive charges results in a stronger attraction between oppositely charged regions, it could increase the likelihood of lightning strikes or result in more powerful lightning, as the energy released in overcoming the insulation properties of the air would be greater.\n\nThus, the perturbation could have both direct and indirect effects on the lightning process, but the outcome would depend on various factors, such as the distribution of positive charges in the cloud and the ground."}]}
