nsport.\n\nOn the other hand, small cells, or class B cells, do not face the same challenges as large cells regarding surface area to volume ratio. Their smaller size allows for adequate nutrient and material transport without the need for additional cell protrusions such as microvilli.\n\nTherefore, class B cells (small cells) are less likely to have microvilli as a feature compared to class A cells (large cells)."}]}
