hots (with fill in actors) and add them to the timeline to see how it looked. Of course no one else was interested in spending an entire night shooting the film – but with them as stands in – just so I could complete my psychotic endeavour of... What did the narrator have story boarded? Pick the correct answer from the following options: - all the shots he needed - not enough information - all the extras he needed - all the actors he needed\nAnswer:"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The narrator had storyboarded all the shots he needed. In the given text, it is mentioned that \"As the neurotic freak I am, I had all the shots I wanted to use storyboarded.\" This indicates that the narrator had planned and visualized all the necessary shots for the film through storyboarding."}]}
